@startuml Candidate State Machine

title Candidate Lifecycle - State Diagram

[*] --> Open : Candidate submits\napplication

state "Open" as Open
state "Scheduled" as Scheduled
state "Pending" as Pending
state "Accepted" as Accepted
state "Rejected" as Rejected

Open --> Scheduled : Schedule interview

Scheduled --> Pending : Interview conducted

Pending --> Accepted : Approve candidate\n[Meets requirements]

Pending --> Rejected : Reject candidate\n[Does not meet requirements]

Scheduled --> Scheduled : Reschedule interview

Open --> Rejected : Reject without\ninterview\n[Does not meet\nminimum requirements]

Accepted --> [*] : Convert to Volunteer\n(Creates new Volunteer entity)

Rejected --> [*] : Archive candidate\n(No volunteer created)

note left of Open
  **Triggers:**
  - Candidate registration
  - Form submission
  
  **Actions:**
  - Validate application
  - Publish to "candidate_updates" topic
end note

note right of Scheduled
  **Triggers:**
  - Coordinator schedules interview
  
  **Actions:**
  - Create interview record
  - Publish to "schedule_updates" topic
end note

note right of Pending
  **Triggers:**
  - Interview completion
  
  **Actions:**
  - Store interview notes
  - Update timestamp
  - Await coordinator decision
end note

note right of Accepted
  **Triggers:**
  - Coordinator approval
  
  **Actions:**
  - Create new Volunteer entity
  - Copy candidate data to volunteer
  - Publish to "campaign_volunteer_updates" topic
end note

note left of Rejected
  **Triggers:**
  - Coordinator rejection
  
  **Actions:**
  - Archive candidate record
  - NO volunteer entity created
  - Publish to "candidate_updates" topic
end note

@enduml
